# What a screen reader reaches of the graph canvas (dynamics grammar plan,
# G9: F62, F65 to F68), read from the page's own semantic tree
# (graphshellSemanticTree), not from the app's state. The canvas slot is a
# group named "N of M shown"; each item on screen is a group whose Drag and
# Pin are buttons, named by label and described by their explanation. A
# reader's Pin pins the item; a reader's Drag starts a keyboard move the
# arrows steer, Enter drops by role and Escape puts back. The positive
# controls run this receipt with ?plant_a11y=missing_item, missing_action and
# dead_action, and each must fail.
assert snap ready == true
settle 3
assert snap reader-canvas == 11 of 11 shown
assert snap reader-items == 11
assert snap reader-buttons ~ Alice:Drag+Pin
assert snap reader-buttons ~ Reference notes:Drag+Pin
assert snap reader-described == 22
reader-click Alice | Pin
settle 2
assert snap pinned ~ Alice
reader-click Reference notes | Drag
settle 1
assert snap key-moving == true
key ArrowRight
settle 1
key ArrowRight
settle 1
assert snap key-move-offset == 84,0
key Enter
settle 2
assert snap key-moving == false
assert snap key-move-offset == 84,0
reader-click Reference notes | Drag
settle 1
key ArrowDown
settle 1
assert snap key-move-offset == 0,42
key Escape
settle 2
assert snap key-moving == false
assert snap key-move-offset == 0,0
capture canvas_reader
wait
log canvas reader receipt complete
